infographic compare-binary-horizontal-underline-text-vs
data
  title N+1 per-row loop vs one set-based query
  desc Loading 1,000 related rows — 1,000 round trips and ~100x slower, or one query pushed into the engine
  compares
    - label N+1 query (per-row loop)
      children
        - label 1,000 round trips for 1,000 rows
          desc One query fired per row, looped in app code
        - label ~100x slower in production
          desc Network latency paid 1,000 times over
        - label 81 queries to load 1 order
          desc 1 parent query + one per line-item (80 items)
        - label Pulls rows up, loops outside
          desc The single most common production perf bug
    - label Set-based query (one JOIN)
      children
        - label 1 round trip for 1,000 rows
          desc WHERE / JOIN fetches the whole set at once
        - label Operation runs inside the engine
          desc Filter and join applied to the set conceptually in parallel
        - label 1 query replaces all 81
          desc One JOIN pulls the order and all 80 items together
        - label Pushes work down where it belongs
          desc Thinking in sets, not per-row loops
theme
  palette #f43f5e #14b8a6
